    "title": "pandas.Series.dtype — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1661.gf74cda2e6e documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.dtype#\n\n- property Series.dtype[source]#\n- Return the dtype object of the underlying data. This is the dtype of the array backing the Series (or the single dtype for a DataFrame column). For extension types, it returns the corresponding extension dtype. See also \n  - `Series.dtypes`\n  - Return the dtype object of the underlying data.\n  - `Series.astype`\n  - Cast a pandas object to a specified dtype dtype.\n  - `Series.convert_dtypes`\n  - Convert columns to the best possible dtypes using dtypes supporting pd.NA.\n Examples >>> s = pd.Series([1, 2, 3]) >>> s.dtype dtype('int64')",
